/TEMP/
.idea
/.idea/
/venv-nlp/
# Recursive, not "/__pycache__/": running the suite drops one of these next to
# every package it imports (tests/, api_util/, service/, annotation/, utils/),
# so an anchored rule leaves the tree full of untracked bytecode dirs after any
# `pytest` run. Matches page-classification's .gitignore, which took the same
# fix on 2026-07-22 (atrium-project#10).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# pytest / coverage scratch. CONTRIBUTING.md's "Running the test suite" documents
# `pytest -m "not slow" --cov=. --cov-report=term-missing`, so following the repo's own
# instructions used to leave three untracked artefacts behind (atrium-project#10).
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
